  "written_by": "just stored-form, at v0.14.0. src/encode/ is byte-identical from v0.12.0 to v0.14.0, and metering 0.23 (under 0.12.0 and 0.13.0) and 0.24 (under 0.14.0) spell every stored vocabulary identically, so this one file is what all three wrote. The fixture's Marktpartner-ID is one whose check digit holds, as every issued one does.",
  "broken_by": [
    {
      "release": "0.15.0",
      "removed": "every AUTO_SUBSTITUTE row (its method is metering 0.25's vee::substitute::Method, whose codes replace LINEAR_INTERPOLATION, PRIOR_PERIOD_AVERAGE, ZERO_FILL and LAST_VALUE_CARRY_FORWARD), and every resolution spelled in seconds (PT1S, PT60S, PT300S: a grid is whole minutes dividing the hour)",
      "not_recorded_here": "a Marktpartner-ID failing both check-digit procedures, in source_detail or version_scope, no longer decodes either; this file's rows carry an issued code and predate the version_scope column, so no row is removed for it",
      "recorded_in": "CHANGELOG.md, 0.15.0, Stored-data break"
    }
  ],
